WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.780
FedRAMP Moderate is an ongoing program commitment rather than a one-time documentation project.

2
00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:14.360
Authorization work may focus attention on a package and an assessment, but the service still needs continuous monitoring after that point.

3
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:25.980
Security posture changes as vulnerabilities are discovered, configurations drift, personnel change, incidents occur, dependencies evolve, and new features alter the system boundary.

4
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:42.900
Continuous monitoring includes vulnerability management, configuration monitoring, change management, incident reporting expectations at a high level, periodic evidence updates, risk tracking, plans of action and milestones, security metrics, and operational ownership.

5
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:51.960
The exact routines may vary, but the principle is stable: the provider must keep visibility into whether controls remain effective and whether risk is changing.

6
00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:55.680
Operational discipline is what keeps Moderate from becoming stale.

7
00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:58.900
Vulnerabilities need owners and timelines.

8
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.080
Significant changes need review.

9
00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:03.180
Monitoring alerts need triage.

10
00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:06.240
Incidents need defined escalation and records.

11
00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:07.940
Evidence needs maintenance.

12
00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.800
Risk items need tracking.

13
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.820
If these activities are disconnected, the security program becomes brittle.

14
00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:19.760
If they are integrated into normal operations, the Moderate baseline becomes sustainable.

15
00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:23.320
Continuous monitoring also supports agency trust.

16
00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:30.380
Federal customers and authorizing officials are not only interested in whether a service looked acceptable at one point in time.

17
00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:39.680
They need confidence that the provider can operate the service responsibly over time, identify problems, communicate risk, and remediate issues.

18
00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:45.380
That is why Moderate should be understood as a living operational model, not a static milestone.
